  "reason": "Evidence: With pca_n2000 + imagenet_vit_l in multiprofile, we have three of four cells in an aggregation×fusion factorial: avgpool+concat=0.6287 (config_010), transformer+concat=0.5988 (config_039), avgpool+weighted=0.6352 (config_026, current best). The missing cell is transformer+weighted (config_001). Question: Does the avgpool-over-transformer advantage (~3 pts) hold independently of fusion, and does the weighted-over-concat advantage (~0.7 pt) hold independently of aggregation? Completing this 2×2 factorial isolates the main effects and reveals any interaction, which is critical before committing further budget to either aggregation or fusion choices. Why this is the best next experiment: It is a single-variable change from the current best (config_026: avgpool→transformer), it is a single-variable change from config_039 (concat→weighted), and it directly tests whether the current best configuration is truly optimal within this encoder pair or whether transformer+weighted could close or reverse the gap. Under a limited budget, resolving this interaction before exploring new encoders (scvi_n200, resnet50) ensures we build subsequent experiments on a correctly understood baseline."
}

